Subject: Entity Component System and SOP Semantic Fabric Correspondence

Description: Source-linked analysis of ECS as a candidate Cantor runtime and physical data projection. It records useful correspondences, semantic mismatches, constraints, and a bounded evaluation route without selecting ECS as the canonical ontology.

@ [correspondence_uuid] acfec44f-1938-4d58-807d-42860743f244
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] 7c642ead-f205-46e5-9d08-3deb2a6b71b4
@ [source_document] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-05_ecs_semantic_fabric_correspondence\Dictated_ECS_Semantic_Fabric_Correspondence_Source.sop
@ [source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-05_ecs_semantic_fabric_correspondence\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [analysis_status] considered_candidate_projection_not_selected

& [CoreFinding] is positive but layered
  + ECS strongly reinforces separation of stable identity, typed data, and behavior selected by explicit queries
  + that separation fits Cantor compilation, faculty processing, temporal scheduling, and fast deterministic iteration
  + ECS is best treated as an optional runtime, cache, or hardware-oriented projection of canonical SemanticIR and repository state
  + ECS is not sufficient as the canonical semantic graph because ordinary ECS does not inherently preserve contextual relations, n-ary assertions, provenance, uncertainty, truth status, authority, or proof

& [CorrespondenceMap] is explicit
  + ECS Entity corresponds to a runtime handle for one stable SemanticIdentity, TaskContract, CalendarItem, ChangeCapsule, artifact, package, run, or other declared subject
  + ECS Component corresponds to one typed immutable or versioned facet such as role, source generation, contract, state, capability request, schedule, lane cursor, diff classification, proof status, or sensitivity label
  + ECS System corresponds to a typed compiler pass, validator, faculty operation, Planner transition, Weaver projection, rear-review transform, scheduler, query operator, or effect gate
  + ECS World or Registry corresponds to one versioned SemanticEnvironment or admitted repository snapshot
  + ECS Query corresponds to selection of identities satisfying an exact component, contract, scope, and authority conjunction
  + ECS Archetype corresponds to a projection-specific component signature or profile, not an essential semantic class
  + ECS System Schedule corresponds to Planner's dependency DAG and explicit read/write/effect conflict ordering
  + ECS Command Buffer corresponds to proposed transitions or effects accumulated before validation and Observer or EffectBroker commitment
  + ECS Event Stream corresponds to MaterialEvent and ChangeCapsule input records when identities and provenance are preserved
  + ECS Snapshot corresponds only to a declared runtime projection snapshot and not an atomic world-state claim

& [FacultyProjection] is coherent
  + Observer can schedule, reconcile, and admit System returns
  + Honesty can validate identity, attribution, evidence, truth-status, and temporal components
  + Security can validate principal, authority, capability, sensitivity, resource, and effect components
  + Scribe can append component deltas and preserve before and after generations
  + Refiner can compute a minimal component and relation delta under equivalence constraints
  + Weaver can project compatible component bundles and cross-entity relations
  + Planner can order Systems according to dependency, data access, review, and effect constraints
  - never: compile faculties into unconstrained systems whose mutation rights come merely from registration

& [CTPRProjection] is especially strong
  + TaskContract, PlanRevision, CalendarItem, ChangeCapsule, LaneCursor, ReflectionReturn, and CompilerGeneration can be entity kinds or semantic identities projected to entity handles
  + immutable state, lifecycle, time, authority, sensitivity, and provenance can be components
  + prospective, execution, retrospective, join, schedule, invalidation, and replay logic can be systems
  + command buffering naturally models prepared-ahead work and the release barrier
  + system access declarations can expose read/write conflicts and support deterministic scheduling
  + append-only component delta records can project into the semantic event journal

& [SemanticMismatchSet] is non-negotiable
  + component presence does not prove the component's assertion true
  + entity-handle equality does not by itself prove stable semantic identity across generations or worlds
  + component type does not encode source, context, temporal validity, confidence, authority, or proof unless those are explicit fields and relations
  + ordinary binary component attachment cannot directly replace contextual, temporal, n-ary, or hypergraph relations
  + archetype membership does not imply ontology class membership or admissible subtype
  + system registration does not grant capability or effect authority
  + mutable in-place component update conflicts with append-only provenance unless changes emit immutable events and generations
  + cache locality and iteration speed do not establish semantic correctness

& [ProjectionContract] is required before selection
  + every entity handle maps to an exact semantic identity and generation
  + every component maps to one canonical SemanticIR or repository facet and declares source, context, valid time, transaction time, authority status, and proof status when applicable
  + every system declares input query, read set, write proposal set, effect set, preconditions, invariants, outputs, faults, budget, and determinism grade
  + systems write through a versioned command buffer and cannot mutate admitted canonical state directly
  + relational edges that cannot be represented without loss remain in a side graph or relation component with explicit participant identities
  + synchronization, compaction, deletion, and archetype migration preserve event and source correspondence
  + deterministic replay reproduces the same normalized component and relation state

& [EvaluationRoute] is deferred and measurable
  + compare canonical graph traversal with ECS projection query performance on the deterministic CTPR fixture
  + test Planner scheduling and system conflict detection
  + test ChangeCapsule command-buffer admission and stale-generation rejection
  + test component attach, detach, migration, compaction, and replay correspondence
  + measure query latency, update work, memory, cache behavior, proof overhead, and semantic-loss count
  + preserve a graph-only exact fallback
  + reject ECS selection if semantic correspondence, provenance, authority, or replay requires hidden conventions

& [CurrentDisposition] is bounded
  + [conceptual_value] is high
  + [canonical_ontology_status] is rejected_as_insufficient
  + [runtime_projection_status] is promising_deferred_candidate
  + [Rust_projection_status] is plausible_not_implemented
  + [FPGA_projection_status] is plausible_after_semantic_and_hardware_profiles
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
